at="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMI, MANABU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>PIAO CHUN-CHENG</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAMOTO RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE YUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YONEMOTO KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMI MANABU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>PIAO, CHUN-CHENG</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAMOTO, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEMOTO, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMI, MANABU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A primary system (20), comprising a compressor (21), a heat exchanger (30), and an expansion device (22) connected in order to each other, wherein outside air is taken in through a primary inlet duct (23) and supplied from a primary outlet duct (24) to an indoor; a secondary system (40), comprising ducts (43 and 44) connected to both ends of the heat exchanger (30), wherein inside air is taken in through the secondary inlet duct (43) and exhausted to the secondary outlet duct (44); a moisture absorbing part (62) of a dehumidifying mechanism (60) is provided in the primary inlet duct (23) and a moisture releasing part (63) is provided in the secondary inlet duct (43), and a rotor member (61) having solid adsorbent is moved rotatably between the moisture absorbing part (62) and the moisture releasing part (63), whereby air dehumidified through the moisture absorbing part (62) is supplied to the compressor (21).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un climatiseur constitué d'un système primaire (209, comprenant un compresseur (21), un échangeur thermique (30), et un détendeur (22) reliés les uns aux autres, l'air extérieur étant aspiré via un conduit (23) d'entrée primaire et fourni à un environnement intérieur par l'intermédiaire d'un conduit (24) de sortie primaire ; d'un système secondaire (40) comprenant des conduits (43) et (44) connectés aux deux extrémités de l'échangeur thermique (30), l'air intérieur étant aspiré via le conduit (43) d'entrée secondaire puis évacué vers le conduit (44) de sortie secondaire ; d'un élément (62) absorbeur d'humidité d'un déshumidificateur (60) disposé dans le conduit (23) d'entrée primaire et d'un élément (63) de libération d'humidité disposé dans le conduit (43) d'entrée secondaire ; et d'un élément (61) de type rotor comprenant un absorbant solide entraîné en rotation entre l'élément (62) absorbeur d'humidité et l'élément (63) de libération d'humidité, l'air asséché par l'élément (62) absorbeur d'humidité venant alimenter le compresseur (21).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/lega